<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Council of Lithuania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1917">1917</a>–<a href="/years/1920">1920</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Taryba</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lithuania">Lithuania</a>, or Taryba, was the body elected by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vilnius">Vilnius</a> Conference in September 1917, under German occupation, to represent Lithuania. Chaired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antanas-smetona">Antanas Smetona</a>, it signed the Act of Independence on 16 February 1918, and in July 1918 briefly proclaimed a monarchy under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilhelm-karl-duke-of-urach">Mindaugas II</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>'s defeat it formed the first governments and gave way to the Constituent Assembly in 1920.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/council-of-lithuania.jpg" alt="Council of Lithuania" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Template:Aleksandra Jurašaitytė · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Signatarai.Signatories_of_Lithuania.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
